    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Db7bsg1hCv2KPFwMY6tc5L)_\n\n## What\n\n- `org-semantic-binary-install` failed with `Wrong type argument: number-or-marker-p, \"Killed: 9\"`.\n  - macOS SIGKILLed the freshly copied binary when the installer ran `--version`.\n  - `process-file` returns a string on a signal, and the package calls `zerop` on it.\n- `sp-semantic.el` now:\n  - deletes the old binary before an install, so the new copy gets a fresh inode;\n  - wraps `org-semantic-binary-version`: on that error it removes the quarantine flag, signs ad hoc (`codesign --force --sign -`), and retries once;\n  - installs the binary under `var/org-semantic/` (git-ignored) instead of the top of the config.\n- The 40 MB binary was tracked in the repo and symlinked by Stow, so installs wrote through the symlink into the repo. It is deleted from the tree here.\n- Doc updated in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-semantic.org` (bullet list) with the tangled `.el`.\n\n## After merging\n\n- Remove the dangling symlink `~/.config/emacs-modular/org-semantic/org-semantic` (and the empty dir), restow, then run `M-x org-semantic-binary-install`.\n\n## Not tested\n\n- Emacs and macOS are not available in the container, so none of this was run.\n- The upstream bug (`zerop` on `process-file`) is in alberti42/org-semantic and is only worked around here.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edits (nightly tidy).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiC5uLeAPStRe4rsvLj)_",
